1
00:00:34,577 --> 00:00:37,496
Stay right where you are.
Danger lurks on every side.

2
00:00:37,580 --> 00:00:39,206
A crew member will be here soon.

3
00:00:39,290 --> 00:00:41,959
You could spill hot oil
or cut yourself if you move.

4
00:00:42,752 --> 00:00:44,462
Stay still until you get used to the dark.

5
00:00:46,505 --> 00:00:47,506
Okay.

6
00:01:04,315 --> 00:01:05,858
Do you think

7
00:01:06,942 --> 00:01:08,527
the live show can go on?

8
00:01:08,611 --> 00:01:11,447
-They wouldn't broadcast this.
-This is madness.

9
00:01:11,530 --> 00:01:13,824
They took our phones before we went live.

10
00:01:13,908 --> 00:01:16,660
This is not good at all.

11
00:01:17,369 --> 00:01:19,371
It's so annoying.

12
00:01:19,997 --> 00:01:24,418
It's all sorts of hell,
good gosh, Jesus Christ.

13
00:01:30,174 --> 00:01:33,552
We don't know when power will return,
so we can't use the deep fryer.

14
00:01:33,636 --> 00:01:34,845
For now…

15
00:01:42,645 --> 00:01:45,856
Let's move the hot oil to these woks.

16
00:01:47,983 --> 00:01:49,527
You could get burned,

17
00:01:49,610 --> 00:01:52,196
so keep an eye on every drop
and move slowly.

18
00:01:52,905 --> 00:01:54,323
-Okay.
-Chef.

19
00:01:54,824 --> 00:01:58,244
I'll go find a crew member
and ask for a flashlight.

20
00:01:58,327 --> 00:01:59,370
Sure.

21
00:02:02,790 --> 00:02:05,543
I'm sorry, chefs. We lost power.

22
00:02:05,626 --> 00:02:07,545
Bear with us while we get it fixed.

23
00:02:08,254 --> 00:02:09,964
I know it'll be tough, but keep cooking.

24
00:02:10,047 --> 00:02:11,882
Sorry. I'm really sorry.

25
00:02:34,613 --> 00:02:35,489
Don't worry.

26
00:02:38,534 --> 00:02:40,786
I'll be sure not to cause you any trouble.

27
00:02:50,504 --> 00:02:52,548
My father's name is Kang San.

28
00:02:55,551 --> 00:02:56,468
But I have…

29
00:03:00,472 --> 00:03:01,557
no mother.

30
00:03:07,104 --> 00:03:08,022
Famiglia…

31
00:03:08,689 --> 00:03:10,816
No, I will

32
00:03:11,817 --> 00:03:13,485
win this competition.

33
00:03:18,782 --> 00:03:20,117
Not just for Chef Choi Seung-hyo

34
00:03:20,868 --> 00:03:22,745
who died a wrongful death,

35
00:03:25,414 --> 00:03:26,749
but also for my father…

36
00:03:30,461 --> 00:03:31,462
who died in torment.

37
00:03:43,474 --> 00:03:44,808
Was that the reason?

38
00:03:53,651 --> 00:03:55,194
You're all startled, aren't you?

39
00:03:55,903 --> 00:03:59,239
We're not going live right now.

40
00:03:59,323 --> 00:04:03,369
Instead, we're broadcasting clips
on Jehyangju for viewers back home.

41
00:04:03,452 --> 00:04:07,289
Try to stay calm.
We were all surprised by the power outage.

42
00:04:07,373 --> 00:04:08,832
THE TABLE: K-CHEF 2026 CHAT ROOM

43
00:04:08,916 --> 00:04:10,292
This is insane.

44
00:04:17,466 --> 00:04:18,300
Yes.

45
00:04:20,260 --> 00:04:21,679
How much longer?

46
00:04:23,472 --> 00:04:24,765
No, we can't wait that long.

47
00:04:27,559 --> 00:04:29,937
Have you lost your mind?
We'd have to pay back all our sponsors.

48
00:04:32,272 --> 00:04:34,525
Wait. The generator truck
powering the audience area…

49
00:04:35,442 --> 00:04:36,735
How far is it to the panelboard?

50
00:04:37,903 --> 00:04:39,780
Yes, the one powering
the lights on the truss.

51
00:04:41,824 --> 00:04:43,826
Turn off the lights in the audience area.

52
00:04:43,909 --> 00:04:46,829
Move the generator truck and connect it
to the second-floor panelboard.

53
00:04:46,912 --> 00:04:47,871
What?

54
00:04:50,290 --> 00:04:52,418
It'll take more time than that.

55
00:04:53,002 --> 00:04:54,628
We can't do that, Ms. Seon.

56
00:04:54,712 --> 00:04:56,714
The lighting team will kill me.

57
00:04:56,797 --> 00:04:59,842
If you don't do as I say,
I'll kill you before they do.

58
00:04:59,925 --> 00:05:01,301
Give it a go. You can do it.

59
00:05:01,385 --> 00:05:02,886
That's our only option. Hurry.

60
00:05:02,970 --> 00:05:04,638
Oh, come on…

61
00:05:05,139 --> 00:05:07,099
Just kill me now.

62
00:05:08,851 --> 00:05:10,227
Operations Crew, listen up.

63
00:05:10,853 --> 00:05:13,397
The lights around the audience area
will go out soon.

64
00:05:17,818 --> 00:05:19,570
We're on a closed set.

65
00:05:19,653 --> 00:05:22,948
The nervous contestants'
warm breath and sweat

66
00:05:23,032 --> 00:05:25,367
are raising the temperature
and the humidity.

67
00:05:39,965 --> 00:05:42,593
If I have to fry the meat in a wok
and not a deep fryer…

68
00:06:12,831 --> 00:06:15,584
The temperature from earlier
is meaningless now.

69
00:06:38,982 --> 00:06:41,652
Remember the pitch and volume
of this sound.

70
00:06:43,487 --> 00:06:44,613
Don't rely only on your sight.

71
00:06:44,696 --> 00:06:46,865
Sometimes, sound is more informative.

72
00:06:46,949 --> 00:06:48,659
And don't trust the thermometer too much.

73
00:06:49,785 --> 00:06:52,454
For this dish, that can be a trap.

74
00:06:54,456 --> 00:06:56,458
What's more important
than focusing on the senses

75
00:06:57,960 --> 00:06:59,586
is what is inside the chef's head.

76
00:07:00,337 --> 00:07:01,296
The big picture.

77
00:07:02,131 --> 00:07:03,340
It's not just about the taste.

78
00:07:04,258 --> 00:07:06,176
Think about the idea you want to express.

79
00:07:06,260 --> 00:07:07,094
That's the point.

80
00:07:09,012 --> 00:07:10,848
Remember just two things in this round.

81
00:07:11,431 --> 00:07:13,183
Memory and imagination.

82
00:07:37,416 --> 00:07:40,836
I wouldn't say I learned
how to brew Jehyangju.

83
00:07:41,628 --> 00:07:44,756
I dedicated my life to the drink.

84
00:07:48,802 --> 00:07:51,513
It was by my side the whole time.

85
00:07:53,015 --> 00:07:55,976
At times, I loved it.
At other times, I resented it.

86
00:07:57,352 --> 00:07:59,479
When a batch didn't work out,

87
00:07:59,563 --> 00:08:02,608
all the months of work went to waste.

88
00:08:04,359 --> 00:08:05,861
I didn't even want to look at it.

89
00:08:06,361 --> 00:08:09,615
But when the following year came around…

90
00:08:09,698 --> 00:08:11,033
WHAT'S GOING ON?
I'M LOSING INTEREST

91
00:08:11,116 --> 00:08:12,659
WHEN DO I SEE COOKING?
A WASTE OF ELECTRICITY

92
00:08:12,743 --> 00:08:14,036
PLAYING B-ROLL TO COVER THINGS UP?

93
00:08:14,745 --> 00:08:15,913
Stop that!

94
00:08:16,455 --> 00:08:18,790
It's harder to shape
if you knead it too much.

95
00:08:18,874 --> 00:08:19,833
Split them up.

96
00:08:20,709 --> 00:08:21,543
Yes, Chef.

97
00:08:32,387 --> 00:08:34,097
-Egg wash.
-Right.

98
00:08:40,979 --> 00:08:42,397
Apply generously. This side too.

99
00:08:42,481 --> 00:08:43,649
-Yes, Chef.
-Here too.

100
00:08:55,452 --> 00:08:57,287
What do you think, Joshua?

101
00:08:59,331 --> 00:09:00,290
Five more minutes.

102
00:09:00,791 --> 00:09:02,459
Let's add them to the broth then, Chef.

103
00:09:23,689 --> 00:09:25,732
Keep going! A bit more!

104
00:09:26,942 --> 00:09:27,859
Keep going.

105
00:09:28,443 --> 00:09:29,278
A bit further back.

106
00:09:29,945 --> 00:09:31,321
Okay, that's it!

107
00:09:33,240 --> 00:09:34,533
Come here, quick.

108
00:09:36,493 --> 00:09:37,744
Connect it to this.

109
00:09:55,846 --> 00:09:57,639
-It's taking too long.
-Let's go home.

110
00:09:57,723 --> 00:09:59,975
We're about to go live again.

111
00:10:00,058 --> 00:10:02,394
Once the cameras start rolling,

112
00:10:02,477 --> 00:10:07,316
could you please bring up the energy
and enjoy the rest of the competition?

113
00:10:08,275 --> 00:10:09,318
Thank you.

114
00:11:46,123 --> 00:11:48,583
Welcome back, "Honey."

115
00:12:14,860 --> 00:12:15,819
We have 27 minutes left.

116
00:12:16,778 --> 00:12:17,821
Can it be done?

117
00:13:03,366 --> 00:13:04,326
It's perfect.

118
00:13:07,871 --> 00:13:10,874
The texture of the meat and the crunch.

119
00:13:16,087 --> 00:13:17,339
The left is cold-pressed sesame oil.

120
00:13:17,422 --> 00:13:19,549
The right is a mix of that
and cottonseed oil.

121
00:13:19,633 --> 00:13:21,092
How long were they fried for?

122
00:13:21,176 --> 00:13:23,595
For 30 seconds in the first wok,
then 20 seconds in the second one.

123
00:13:23,678 --> 00:13:27,349
I couldn't use the deep fryer,
so I judged the temperature by ear.

124
00:13:27,432 --> 00:13:28,266
And the pickles?

125
00:13:28,850 --> 00:13:30,143
They're soaking in Mount Gyesul water.

126
00:13:30,227 --> 00:13:32,646
Because of the outage,
we don't have time to sous vide them.

127
00:14:14,145 --> 00:14:16,398
We'll add some rub to the fried meat.

128
00:14:17,774 --> 00:14:20,819
Song. Grind everything together
and make a rub.

129
00:14:20,902 --> 00:14:21,987
It has to be very fine.

130
00:14:22,070 --> 00:14:23,989
Think of the rub we applied to the duck.

131
00:14:24,072 --> 00:14:27,617
But this time,
the main isn't cumin but acorn flour.

132
00:14:28,827 --> 00:14:29,661
Don't forget.

133
00:14:30,787 --> 00:14:31,913
The point of today's dish

134
00:14:32,581 --> 00:14:34,874
is the scent of a forest
and the cheonghyang.

135
00:14:35,959 --> 00:14:36,793
Got it.

136
00:14:38,628 --> 00:14:39,796
What can we do to help?

137
00:14:49,139 --> 00:14:51,891
Carve the pickles into petals.

138
00:14:51,975 --> 00:14:53,393
Forget the sous vide.

139
00:14:53,476 --> 00:14:54,936
Make them see-through and thin.

140
00:14:55,020 --> 00:14:56,730
So they look like a flower
when put together?

141
00:14:59,316 --> 00:15:00,609
-Chef Jang.
-Yes, Chef.

142
00:15:00,692 --> 00:15:02,777
You'll coat the petals Chef Cha made.

143
00:15:02,861 --> 00:15:05,196
Turn the wildflower water into a glaze.

144
00:15:05,280 --> 00:15:08,074
-Use wildflower honey, not sugar.
-Got it.

145
00:15:10,160 --> 00:15:11,995
Song, once the rub is done,

146
00:15:12,078 --> 00:15:14,706
load the smoke gun with dry pine needles
and Jehyangju-scented chips.

147
00:15:14,789 --> 00:15:15,915
-Don't forget!
-Okay.

148
00:15:17,917 --> 00:15:18,877
SANGJU DRIED PERSIMMONS

149
00:15:38,396 --> 00:15:39,230
You're aware, right?

150
00:15:42,275 --> 00:15:44,361
Our goal isn't just to pass this round.

151
00:16:09,928 --> 00:16:11,429
How much time do we have left, Su-in?

152
00:16:11,971 --> 00:16:13,098
Just 9 minutes and 20 seconds.

153
00:16:18,061 --> 00:16:21,356
Isabel. It's getting close.
Need to speed up.

154
00:16:21,439 --> 00:16:23,066
Yeah, sure thing.

155
00:16:36,746 --> 00:16:37,580
It's ready.

156
00:17:18,955 --> 00:17:22,709
Being strong isn't about sheer willpower,
but about the life energy within us.

157
00:17:37,849 --> 00:17:40,727
This food will give you
a strong life force.

158
00:17:40,810 --> 00:17:43,563
Being strong isn't about
fighting and winning.

159
00:17:45,648 --> 00:17:46,649
Always be grateful.

160
00:17:47,650 --> 00:17:50,987
Nature always gives us a new gift.

161
00:19:51,566 --> 00:19:55,111
BINGSAK / GOLDEN DRAGON
MEMORIES OF SWIPING EGGS

162
00:19:55,904 --> 00:19:56,821
Our team

163
00:19:58,031 --> 00:20:01,910
took tteokbokki and sundae,
the most common street food,

164
00:20:02,660 --> 00:20:05,830
and reinvented them
using Western cooking techniques.

165
00:20:05,914 --> 00:20:08,416
The idea was to elevate
the most common snack food

166
00:20:09,876 --> 00:20:11,711
by preparing and presenting them

167
00:20:12,670 --> 00:20:15,632
like something you'd see
in a high-end restaurant.

168
00:20:18,426 --> 00:20:20,094
When I was a little boy,

169
00:20:21,179 --> 00:20:23,765
I stole lots of chickens and eggs.

170
00:20:24,265 --> 00:20:27,602
I would make soup with the chicken
and boil eggs.

171
00:20:28,561 --> 00:20:30,688
It was so good.

172
00:20:31,230 --> 00:20:33,399
I wanted to capture
and share that feeling.

173
00:20:36,819 --> 00:20:38,154
Oh my gosh.

174
00:20:45,078 --> 00:20:46,829
There's actual tteokbokki inside.

175
00:20:47,580 --> 00:20:48,748
It's not bad.

176
00:20:49,290 --> 00:20:50,249
Nice and crunchy.

177
00:20:55,463 --> 00:20:58,257
Technically, it was stealing.

178
00:20:58,925 --> 00:21:01,094
But the good old days
become fond memories, right?

179
00:21:07,725 --> 00:21:11,396
BINGSAK / GOLDEN DRAGON
RICE OR BREAD? THAT IS THE QUESTION

180
00:21:12,146 --> 00:21:14,107
I always felt torn at lunchtime.

181
00:21:15,650 --> 00:21:18,778
If someone had bread, I wanted bread.

182
00:21:18,861 --> 00:21:21,572
So if I ate bread,
I craved rice with something.

183
00:21:22,281 --> 00:21:24,492
If I ate rice, I wanted bread instead.

184
00:21:28,830 --> 00:21:31,666
So I made something
to satisfy both cravings.

185
00:21:41,718 --> 00:21:43,845
The problem was the alcohol.

186
00:21:44,345 --> 00:21:48,391
It was difficult to find the right harmony
between the strong flavors of street food

187
00:21:48,474 --> 00:21:51,060
and the light aroma of cheongju.

188
00:21:51,644 --> 00:21:52,478
So…

189
00:21:53,813 --> 00:21:56,691
We decided to be bold…

190
00:21:59,068 --> 00:22:00,695
and give the liquor a twist.

191
00:22:00,778 --> 00:22:03,906
That was Dragon-Sak's strategy.

192
00:22:06,701 --> 00:22:07,910
To put it simply,

193
00:22:08,578 --> 00:22:09,704
we made cocktails.

194
00:22:09,787 --> 00:22:13,332
A unique pairing with a cocktail
made with traditional Korean liquor.

195
00:22:14,333 --> 00:22:17,462
We used strawberry wine
and green tangerine wine

196
00:22:18,254 --> 00:22:19,630
to make our own creations.

197
00:22:22,258 --> 00:22:24,135
Jehyangju cocktails, if you will.

198
00:22:24,761 --> 00:22:26,095
Ta-da.

199
00:22:32,435 --> 00:22:35,063
That's what we came up with.

200
00:22:41,277 --> 00:22:44,947
HUSH / ONGOJISIM
THIS IS NOT GIMBAP

201
00:22:46,741 --> 00:22:47,950
Cheongju.

202
00:22:49,368 --> 00:22:51,746
What would be the perfect spread
to go with cheongju,

203
00:22:51,829 --> 00:22:53,790
the traditional Korean wine?

204
00:22:55,458 --> 00:22:58,127
We focused on Jehyangju's main ingredient.

205
00:22:58,628 --> 00:23:00,630
It's rice.

206
00:23:02,131 --> 00:23:04,383
We decided to use rice
as our key ingredient too.

207
00:23:04,467 --> 00:23:05,468
You may have guessed it.

208
00:23:06,344 --> 00:23:07,512
We made gimbap.

209
00:23:26,030 --> 00:23:28,449
SANGJU RICE

210
00:23:28,533 --> 00:23:31,577
Koreans call food "bap,"
which is also the word for cooked rice.

211
00:23:31,661 --> 00:23:35,957
It shows how important rice is
to Korean cuisine in general.

212
00:23:37,625 --> 00:23:40,128
Cooked rice is basically rice,

213
00:23:40,753 --> 00:23:43,172
and Jehyangju is also made with rice.

214
00:23:43,256 --> 00:23:46,676
We put all our efforts into making

215
00:23:47,260 --> 00:23:48,302
the tastiest rice.

216
00:23:50,221 --> 00:23:51,806
Food made with rice

217
00:23:52,723 --> 00:23:54,267
and wine made with rice.

218
00:23:56,394 --> 00:23:58,229
Could there ever be a better match?

219
00:24:09,991 --> 00:24:11,284
HUSH / ONGOJISIM
A BLESSING FOR ALL

220
00:24:11,367 --> 00:24:13,661
I prepared a bowl of noodles.

221
00:24:14,287 --> 00:24:17,123
This broth brings back
fond memories for me.

222
00:24:18,082 --> 00:24:21,377
The most important ingredient
is large anchovies.

223
00:24:21,460 --> 00:24:24,755
I used a cooking technique
straight from my childhood.

224
00:24:24,839 --> 00:24:27,758
I smoked sunray surf clams
with coal briquette pieces

225
00:24:27,842 --> 00:24:29,302
before adding them to the broth.

226
00:24:29,385 --> 00:24:30,887
The jelly you see

227
00:24:30,970 --> 00:24:34,765
was made with swimming anemones
caught along the Haeon coast.

228
00:24:34,849 --> 00:24:37,518
I wanted to serve a warm broth

229
00:24:37,602 --> 00:24:40,188
to accompany the cold, light cheongju.

230
00:24:41,147 --> 00:24:43,107
I'm sure you were all the same,

231
00:24:43,191 --> 00:24:47,528
but I was mischievous and curious
when I was in elementary school.

232
00:24:48,237 --> 00:24:51,032
Looking back on the days
I spent having fun

233
00:24:51,115 --> 00:24:54,285
made me want to add some fun to the food.

234
00:24:54,869 --> 00:24:57,538
We made a plate with cooked noodles

235
00:24:57,622 --> 00:24:59,624
and placed a slab of jelly on top.

236
00:25:23,147 --> 00:25:25,650
I hope you enjoy the trip back in time.

237
00:25:35,201 --> 00:25:37,036
Cheongju is made with rice.

238
00:25:37,703 --> 00:25:40,498
It belongs to us and no one else.

239
00:25:41,082 --> 00:25:42,500
The clear and noble taste

240
00:25:43,292 --> 00:25:44,585
and the light aroma.

241
00:25:45,169 --> 00:25:47,922
It represents us as a people.

242
00:25:48,798 --> 00:25:51,425
I was reminded of how much
our traditional liquors mean to us

243
00:25:52,635 --> 00:25:54,470
and how great they are

244
00:25:54,553 --> 00:25:57,848
through this mission with Jehyangju.

245
00:26:04,730 --> 00:26:05,773
Thank you

246
00:26:06,774 --> 00:26:09,193
for giving us the chance
to give cheongju its name back.

247
00:26:14,115 --> 00:26:16,450
HOME-STYLE KOREAN RESTAURANT

248
00:26:16,534 --> 00:26:20,288
It is now time to reveal the last spread.

249
00:26:21,289 --> 00:26:25,084
-Team Famiglia-Exception.
-Can we have two set meals?

250
00:26:25,167 --> 00:26:26,877
Please come to the stage.

251
00:26:26,961 --> 00:26:28,296
FINAL SPREAD REVEAL
FAMIGLIA / EXCEPTION

252
00:26:31,048 --> 00:26:31,882
Ma'am.

253
00:26:33,759 --> 00:26:34,760
Hello?

254
00:26:36,429 --> 00:26:38,222
Two set meals, please.

255
00:26:38,306 --> 00:26:40,391
What's got you so hooked?

256
00:26:41,809 --> 00:26:44,312
Sorry. We're closed for the day.

257
00:26:44,395 --> 00:26:45,980
What? Already?

258
00:26:46,605 --> 00:26:47,523
This early?

259
00:26:49,108 --> 00:26:51,235
We're out of ingredients.

260
00:26:51,319 --> 00:26:55,906
What diner runs out of ingredients
right around dinnertime?

261
00:26:55,990 --> 00:26:57,658
-Let's go somewhere else.
-Okay.

262
00:26:57,742 --> 00:26:58,659
We'll come back later.

263
00:26:58,743 --> 00:27:01,120
Okay. Sorry.

264
00:27:01,203 --> 00:27:04,040
-The food here is good though.
-What a shame.

265
00:27:08,127 --> 00:27:10,421
Team Famiglia-Exception.

266
00:27:10,504 --> 00:27:12,506
What did you prepare for us today?

267
00:27:13,507 --> 00:27:15,259
The dish I made today is…

268
00:27:16,135 --> 00:27:17,094
jjondeugi.

269
00:27:18,179 --> 00:27:21,766
EXCEPTION / FAMIGLIA
MY CHILDHOOD JJONDEUGI

270
00:27:21,849 --> 00:27:24,310
Street food we enjoyed as kids

271
00:27:24,393 --> 00:27:26,354
and liquor we get to try as adults.

272
00:27:27,104 --> 00:27:30,274
What's more, we had to work
with traditional Korean liquor.

273
00:27:31,650 --> 00:27:33,027
It's harder than you think.

274
00:27:34,862 --> 00:27:38,491
It's because none of us
had come across that pairing.

275
00:27:40,076 --> 00:27:44,205
Finding a commonality between the two.

276
00:27:46,582 --> 00:27:47,666
That was the key.

277
00:27:55,174 --> 00:27:56,092
Looking back…

278
00:27:58,469 --> 00:27:59,345
on our memories.

279
00:28:02,640 --> 00:28:05,393
That's where I think the two meet.

280
00:28:06,769 --> 00:28:09,271
I hoped to connect
the subtle aroma of rice in the cheongju

281
00:28:09,355 --> 00:28:12,525
to memories of a dish
I enjoyed as a child.

282
00:28:13,442 --> 00:28:15,611
Whether happy or painful,

283
00:28:16,695 --> 00:28:18,489
those memories are

284
00:28:19,740 --> 00:28:20,783
all part of our past.

285
00:28:21,826 --> 00:28:24,453
Looking back on our memories…

286
00:28:25,246 --> 00:28:30,418
24 YEARS AGO,
YOUNG CULINARY TALENT COMPETITION

287
00:28:31,502 --> 00:28:32,711
CHA WOO-JIN

288
00:28:57,111 --> 00:28:58,279
SEOAN ELEMENTARY
GRADE 5, CLASS 2

289
00:28:58,362 --> 00:29:01,615
The taste and smell of rice
are part of our very being.

290
00:29:01,699 --> 00:29:04,410
So I took the Western dish rollatini

291
00:29:04,994 --> 00:29:07,997
and made it with rice flour
and cornstarch instead of wheat flour.

292
00:29:08,581 --> 00:29:12,918
I based its shape and color
on our childhood favorite, jjondeugi.

293
00:29:13,502 --> 00:29:15,880
The exceptionally sweet
Shine Muscat grapes from Sangju

294
00:29:15,963 --> 00:29:18,007
give the sauce
an extra touch of sweetness.

295
00:29:40,196 --> 00:29:41,489
She's still the same?

296
00:29:41,572 --> 00:29:42,406
YEAR 2006

297
00:29:42,490 --> 00:29:44,658
Yes. She won't even touch it.

298
00:29:45,159 --> 00:29:47,578
This is just dreadful.

299
00:29:47,661 --> 00:29:49,914
We might have to organize another funeral.

300
00:29:49,997 --> 00:29:51,749
I hope she eats some gruel at least.

301
00:29:51,832 --> 00:29:54,001
-What should we do?
-I don't know.

302
00:29:54,793 --> 00:29:57,713
She hasn't eaten in days,
and I'm getting worried.

303
00:29:57,796 --> 00:29:59,840
She must be heartbroken.

304
00:30:00,591 --> 00:30:04,303
She lost both her husband
and son overnight.

305
00:30:35,209 --> 00:30:36,293
It's oyster tteokguk.

306
00:30:38,671 --> 00:30:39,630
I hope you stay strong.

307
00:30:56,605 --> 00:30:57,856
I hope this dish

308
00:30:59,066 --> 00:31:00,985
brings back some fond memories

309
00:31:02,486 --> 00:31:03,904
from your happy times.

310
00:31:08,284 --> 00:31:10,703
Looking back in time…

311
00:31:11,870 --> 00:31:13,581
and memories I cannot erase.

312
00:32:48,008 --> 00:32:51,428
What did you prepare this time,
Chef Chris?

313
00:32:52,888 --> 00:32:54,014
The second dish

314
00:32:54,598 --> 00:32:55,557
is gangjeong.

315
00:33:05,567 --> 00:33:08,028
EXCEPTION / FAMIGLIA
WILDFOWL GANGJEONG WITH CHEONGHYANG

316
00:33:08,112 --> 00:33:09,238
Gangjeong?

317
00:33:09,863 --> 00:33:13,617
Did you just say "gangjeong," Chef Chris?

318
00:33:13,701 --> 00:33:14,576
Yes.

319
00:33:15,452 --> 00:33:18,914
The very gangjeong
that makes you think of fried chicken.

320
00:33:30,884 --> 00:33:31,927
This gangjeong

321
00:33:32,678 --> 00:33:34,763
was made with the meat of wildfowl.

322
00:33:38,016 --> 00:33:40,102
-Wildfowl?
-Yes.

323
00:33:40,185 --> 00:33:42,980
We mixed wildfowl meat with chicken.

324
00:33:43,063 --> 00:33:45,566
Quail and pheasant, to be exact.

325
00:33:46,567 --> 00:33:48,152
We also added wild vegetables

326
00:33:48,235 --> 00:33:50,821
such as deodeok
for extra taste and flavor.

327
00:33:50,904 --> 00:33:53,741
To enhance the texture
and bring back a sweetness you remember,

328
00:33:53,824 --> 00:33:56,869
we added diced pieces
of dried persimmon from Sangju.

329
00:33:57,453 --> 00:33:59,288
The crust is glutinous rice flour.

330
00:33:59,371 --> 00:34:01,123
We fried it once
in cold-pressed sesame oil

331
00:34:01,206 --> 00:34:04,001
and then in a blend of
cold-pressed sesame and cottonseed oils.

332
00:34:04,084 --> 00:34:05,294
By deep-frying twice,

333
00:34:05,377 --> 00:34:08,172
we maximized the aroma and crunch.

334
00:34:08,756 --> 00:34:12,134
After we fried it, we applied a rub
made with various spices.

335
00:34:13,594 --> 00:34:16,638
The main ingredient of the rub
was acorn flour.

336
00:34:17,598 --> 00:34:18,557
Acorns?

337
00:34:34,406 --> 00:34:37,951
The gangjeong is served
with a lotus root and lotus seed purée.

338
00:34:38,035 --> 00:34:43,081
We did our best to incorporate the scent
of Jehyangju's lotus blossoms in the food.

339
00:34:43,874 --> 00:34:47,002
That's because we believed
the lotus flower scent

340
00:34:47,085 --> 00:34:49,505
was the cheonghyang
our ancestors spoke of.

341
00:34:54,468 --> 00:34:56,011
Just as you explained,

342
00:34:56,094 --> 00:34:58,639
your food gives off
a set of interesting aromas.

343
00:34:58,722 --> 00:35:00,933
That includes what I noticed
when the lid came off.

344
00:35:01,892 --> 00:35:05,813
The aroma that envelops this dish.

345
00:35:06,396 --> 00:35:11,443
Is it the cheonghyang
that your team tried to recreate?

346
00:35:16,865 --> 00:35:17,908
That's right.

347
00:35:17,991 --> 00:35:20,828
We tried to capture the scent
of lotus flowers from Jehyangju

348
00:35:20,911 --> 00:35:24,122
and the smell of a forest.

349
00:35:30,212 --> 00:35:32,965
We soaked maple-wood chips in Jehyangju

350
00:35:33,048 --> 00:35:34,842
and burned them to create smoke.

351
00:35:35,342 --> 00:35:38,011
The vegetables were pickled
in water from Mount Gyesul.

352
00:35:38,095 --> 00:35:39,847
The finishing oils

353
00:35:39,930 --> 00:35:42,641
were lotus flower oil and pine needle oil.

354
00:35:58,574 --> 00:36:02,327
I would like to turn your attention
to the Jehyangju served with the rollatini

355
00:36:03,412 --> 00:36:07,499
and then to the Jehyangju
served with the wildfowl gangjeong.

356
00:36:22,806 --> 00:36:23,807
These two shots

357
00:36:25,142 --> 00:36:27,060
are actually different liquors.

358
00:36:34,443 --> 00:36:36,653
JEHYANGJU

359
00:36:45,287 --> 00:36:47,205
BOTTLED IN SEPTEMBER 2025

360
00:36:49,207 --> 00:36:51,376
BOTTLED IN MARCH 2025

361
00:36:51,960 --> 00:36:53,337
The shot with the first dish

362
00:36:54,212 --> 00:36:56,798
began maturing in November,
just when it started to get cold.

363
00:36:57,424 --> 00:36:58,884
It withstood the cold winter months.

364
00:36:59,593 --> 00:37:01,970
It has a subdued, dry taste.

365
00:37:06,224 --> 00:37:07,100
The second shot

366
00:37:08,143 --> 00:37:09,978
was matured in the spring month of April.

367
00:37:10,687 --> 00:37:13,357
It survived the hot summer months.

368
00:37:14,066 --> 00:37:16,777
Naturally, that makes it sweeter.

369
00:37:17,903 --> 00:37:20,405
These two shots have different memories.

370
00:37:21,073 --> 00:37:25,369
One remembers a winter
when everything disappears in beauty.

371
00:37:26,036 --> 00:37:28,205
The other remembers a spring

372
00:37:29,539 --> 00:37:31,083
when life returns.

373
00:37:32,417 --> 00:37:33,502
There is no right answer.

374
00:37:34,419 --> 00:37:35,379
But we chose to serve

375
00:37:36,004 --> 00:37:39,758
a seafood dish to go with a wine
that matured during the winter.

376
00:37:41,218 --> 00:37:44,638
As for the wine bottled in September
that has more body,

377
00:37:45,347 --> 00:37:48,767
we paired it with wildfowl gangjeong
that has a rich, meaty flavor.

378
00:37:52,854 --> 00:37:53,981
Today's special star

379
00:37:55,649 --> 00:37:56,775
isn't the food.

380
00:37:58,652 --> 00:37:59,903
It's that liquor.

381
00:38:05,575 --> 00:38:06,827
I hope those two shots of wine…

382
00:38:09,121 --> 00:38:10,539
make you think about the force

383
00:38:12,249 --> 00:38:13,583
that makes all life disappear…

384
00:38:15,544 --> 00:38:17,004
but also reappear.

385
00:38:18,630 --> 00:38:19,923
Time.

386
00:38:52,080 --> 00:38:56,043
It's time to announce the final ranking.

387
00:39:31,119 --> 00:39:33,455
The Table: K-Chef 2026.

388
00:39:33,538 --> 00:39:36,500
The third round, "You are my destiny."

389
00:39:37,250 --> 00:39:40,295
I'll announce the team
to be eliminated in this round.

390
00:40:02,567 --> 00:40:04,653
The team to be eliminated is…

391
00:40:08,240 --> 00:40:09,116
It is…

392
00:40:09,616 --> 00:40:11,868
THE TABLE: K-CHEF 2026

393
00:40:46,611 --> 00:40:48,363
ROUND 3 ELIMINATION
BINGSAK / GOLDEN DRAGON

394
00:40:49,406 --> 00:40:51,032
ROUND 3 WINNER

395
00:40:51,116 --> 00:40:52,576
ROUND 3 WINNER
FAMIGLIA / EXCEPTION

396
00:41:08,300 --> 00:41:09,301
We did it.

397
00:41:46,796 --> 00:41:48,673
THE TABLE: K-CHEF 2026
ROUND 3: YOU ARE MY DESTINY

398
00:41:48,757 --> 00:41:51,718
BINGSAK, GOLDEN DRAGON: ELIMINATED

399
00:41:51,801 --> 00:41:56,723
THE TABLE: K-CHEF 2026
ROUND 4 THEME

400
00:42:07,400 --> 00:42:08,652
I hope these two shots of wine…

401
00:42:11,613 --> 00:42:13,031
make you think about the force…

402
00:42:15,825 --> 00:42:17,160
that makes all life disappear

403
00:42:18,245 --> 00:42:19,454
but also reappear.

404
00:42:21,498 --> 00:42:22,832
Time.

405
00:42:24,751 --> 00:42:26,002
The force that makes all life

406
00:42:26,920 --> 00:42:28,672
disappear and also reappear.

407
00:42:30,632 --> 00:42:31,508
Time.

408
00:42:44,271 --> 00:42:46,815
Why am I craving a drink right now?

409
00:43:07,377 --> 00:43:09,004
Don't think. Just drink.

410
00:43:33,862 --> 00:43:34,696
Wow.

411
00:43:36,448 --> 00:43:37,615
It's sweet.

412
00:43:39,784 --> 00:43:40,994
It's really sweet.

413
00:43:42,996 --> 00:43:43,997
Is it because of my mood?

414
00:44:24,996 --> 00:44:26,706
That was to celebrate us.

415
00:44:33,713 --> 00:44:36,007
I know the past few days
have been rough for you.

416
00:44:49,896 --> 00:44:50,897
Thank you…

417
00:44:53,525 --> 00:44:54,484
for coming back.

418
00:45:17,799 --> 00:45:19,259
My poor back.

419
00:45:20,218 --> 00:45:23,054
I should be done
once I clear out this side.

420
00:45:23,555 --> 00:45:24,639
What about you?

421
00:45:24,722 --> 00:45:27,058
I think this is the last crate for us.

422
00:45:27,142 --> 00:45:29,394
Did you pack the smoke gun?

423
00:45:29,477 --> 00:45:30,854
Yes, I packed it earlier.

424
00:45:31,438 --> 00:45:34,858
I'll handle the rest.
You can take it and get going.

425
00:45:34,941 --> 00:45:37,026
It'll probably take a while
to load the truck.

426
00:45:37,110 --> 00:45:38,486
Guess I could do that.

427
00:45:39,737 --> 00:45:40,822
You did great.

428
00:45:41,906 --> 00:45:44,492
You must've been flustered,
joining the team halfway through.

429
00:45:44,576 --> 00:45:47,829
Thank you so much
for hanging in there until the end.

430
00:45:48,580 --> 00:45:50,206
You too, Chef Choi.

431
00:45:51,416 --> 00:45:54,794
We worked like an actual team, didn't we?

432
00:45:55,587 --> 00:45:56,713
We did.

433
00:45:56,796 --> 00:45:58,506
We are one team.

434
00:46:02,969 --> 00:46:03,928
So…

435
00:46:04,721 --> 00:46:07,265
What do you think the next mission is?

436
00:46:07,348 --> 00:46:08,308
What?

437
00:46:09,184 --> 00:46:12,896
The photos they showed us
for the next round.

438
00:46:15,482 --> 00:46:18,568
A white porcelain vase wrapped in cloth.

439
00:46:19,861 --> 00:46:20,778
White porcelain.

440
00:46:22,071 --> 00:46:22,947
Cloth.

441
00:46:27,619 --> 00:46:29,537
-I'll get going then.
-Okay.

442
00:46:59,901 --> 00:47:00,735
Mr. Park.

443
00:47:01,861 --> 00:47:03,154
You're still here?

444
00:47:04,155 --> 00:47:05,156
What brought you here?

445
00:47:07,408 --> 00:47:09,410
We were packing up. It's a total mess.

446
00:47:22,131 --> 00:47:23,341
JEHYANGJU

447
00:47:27,345 --> 00:47:28,555
Jehyangju is made

448
00:47:30,139 --> 00:47:32,225
with water from Mount Gyesul.

449
00:47:34,352 --> 00:47:36,187
That's why I couldn't expand the business.

450
00:47:37,105 --> 00:47:39,107
I could only use water from Mount Gyesul.

451
00:47:39,732 --> 00:47:41,734
Otherwise, it wouldn't be Jehyangju.

452
00:47:42,527 --> 00:47:43,403
Naturally,

453
00:47:45,196 --> 00:47:46,739
mass production was impossible.

454
00:47:48,116 --> 00:47:48,950
I see.

455
00:47:55,290 --> 00:47:57,875
I've lived here my whole life.

456
00:47:58,960 --> 00:48:00,503
I climbed Mount Gyesul often too.

457
00:48:01,087 --> 00:48:02,005
Almost every day.

458
00:48:03,464 --> 00:48:05,008
It was my playground.

459
00:48:07,385 --> 00:48:08,928
Near Mount Gyesul's peak…

460
00:48:10,680 --> 00:48:12,265
What's it called?

461
00:48:12,890 --> 00:48:13,766
Oh, yes.

462
00:48:14,475 --> 00:48:17,061
There's a temple near the peak.

463
00:48:19,355 --> 00:48:22,400
There used to be one until 30 years ago.

464
00:48:24,235 --> 00:48:27,322
Records say it was built
in the Unified Silla era.

465
00:48:29,282 --> 00:48:30,783
I'm not sure if that's true,

466
00:48:31,743 --> 00:48:35,622
but if it is, the temple was there
for well over a thousand years.

467
00:48:39,292 --> 00:48:41,336
It's burned down now.

468
00:48:43,588 --> 00:48:45,298
There was a huge forest fire, you see.

469
00:48:49,886 --> 00:48:51,554
When we saw the mountain turned to ash,

470
00:48:53,890 --> 00:48:56,184
everyone was brokenhearted.

471
00:48:59,520 --> 00:49:01,439
I cried a lot then.

472
00:49:04,442 --> 00:49:07,320
It was my home, my playground,

473
00:49:08,655 --> 00:49:10,615
my hometown, and my friend.

474
00:49:13,117 --> 00:49:15,328
It felt like I lost it all overnight.

475
00:49:18,873 --> 00:49:20,041
Mount Gyesul

476
00:49:21,125 --> 00:49:22,543
isn't just a mountain.

477
00:49:23,920 --> 00:49:25,630
It's like a parent…

478
00:49:28,049 --> 00:49:29,467
and a friend to us all.

479
00:49:38,601 --> 00:49:39,477
That temple.

480
00:49:41,813 --> 00:49:44,524
The water source right outside
the temple that burned down.

481
00:49:45,942 --> 00:49:47,902
It was covered in lotus flowers.

482
00:49:51,989 --> 00:49:53,616
The monk who built the temple

483
00:49:55,159 --> 00:49:57,745
dug a large pond by the water source

484
00:49:58,538 --> 00:49:59,747
and grew lotus flowers there.

485
00:50:02,542 --> 00:50:03,751
It lives in the mud

486
00:50:04,919 --> 00:50:08,131
but grows such beautiful flowers.

487
00:50:11,467 --> 00:50:13,970
The monk hoped all life
would flourish in this troubled world…

488
00:50:17,098 --> 00:50:19,392
just like the beautiful lotus flowers.

489
00:50:23,730 --> 00:50:24,605
Then…

490
00:50:26,399 --> 00:50:27,358
Jehyangju.

491
00:50:29,902 --> 00:50:32,280
It's made with water from that source.

492
00:50:38,703 --> 00:50:41,456
I'd forgotten for a long time.

493
00:50:44,167 --> 00:50:46,294
We had all forgotten.

494
00:50:47,962 --> 00:50:49,547
The temple is burned and gone,

495
00:50:51,048 --> 00:50:53,092
and the pond once covered in lotus flowers

496
00:50:55,011 --> 00:50:57,930
disappeared from Mount Gyesul long ago.

497
00:50:59,515 --> 00:51:01,350
And from our memories.

498
00:51:04,979 --> 00:51:07,356
But the land and water remembered.

499
00:51:10,735 --> 00:51:12,695
The land and water didn't forget.

500
00:51:14,572 --> 00:51:15,490
The lotus flowers.

501
00:51:18,159 --> 00:51:20,369
The roots and flowers
they had nurtured like their own…

502
00:51:22,663 --> 00:51:24,457
for over a thousand years.

503
00:51:47,355 --> 00:51:49,148
You helped me remember…

504
00:51:51,651 --> 00:51:53,110
what I'd forgotten.

505
00:51:54,737 --> 00:51:56,155
The sad

506
00:51:56,989 --> 00:51:58,282
but precious times

507
00:51:59,283 --> 00:52:00,576
we had forgotten.

508
00:52:08,125 --> 00:52:09,168
Thank you.

509
00:52:45,872 --> 00:52:47,290
-Good night.
-Good job.

510
00:52:57,592 --> 00:52:58,426
Hello?

511
00:52:59,218 --> 00:53:00,803
Hello.

512
00:53:00,887 --> 00:53:04,098
I'm Joo Min-ha,
a journalist with Weekly Celeb.

513
00:53:06,642 --> 00:53:08,603
Hello, Ms. Joo.

514
00:53:08,686 --> 00:53:11,564
Are you Ms. Choi Song-yi, Famiglia's CEO?

515
00:53:13,065 --> 00:53:16,611
Yes, that's me. What's this about?

516
00:53:17,945 --> 00:53:19,655
I want to ask you something.

517
00:53:20,448 --> 00:53:22,992
It came up during today's live show.

518
00:53:24,201 --> 00:53:26,662
The father of your head chef, Chris K.,

519
00:53:27,622 --> 00:53:30,875
is the husband of Pyeongyeon Group's
chairwoman Moon Hae-seon.

520
00:53:30,958 --> 00:53:32,752
Were you aware of that?

521
00:53:33,753 --> 00:53:34,629
What?

522
00:53:35,838 --> 00:53:36,964
By any chance,

523
00:53:38,424 --> 00:53:42,011
is Chris K. Chairwoman Moon's son?

524
00:55:25,031 --> 00:55:27,908
CHRIS K. REVEALED TO BE
GREAT-GRANDSON OF ROYAL HEAD CHEF

525
00:55:31,662 --> 00:55:34,457
TRACING CHRIS K.'S ROOTS:
KANG SAN AND MOON HAE-SEON'S CONNECTION

526
00:55:37,376 --> 00:55:39,879
TRAILS AND BLANKS…
A QUESTION REMAINS ABOUT CHRIS K.

527
00:55:41,714 --> 00:55:44,467
SON GOES LOOKING FOR DAD POST-DIVORCE,
AND BOTH MYSTERIOUSLY DISAPPEAR

528
00:55:57,021 --> 00:55:57,938
Are you packed?

529
00:55:59,774 --> 00:56:02,026
-Well, Chef…
-What are you looking at?

530
00:56:04,987 --> 00:56:06,989
QUESTIONS ARISE ABOUT CHRIS K.'S PARENTAGE

531
00:56:08,032 --> 00:56:09,200
What does this mean?

532
00:56:13,496 --> 00:56:17,041
CHRIS K'S FATHER, KANG SAN,
REVEALED TO BE CHAIRWOMAN MOON'S HUSBAND

533
00:56:19,126 --> 00:56:22,922
IT IS POSSIBLE THAT CHRIS K. IS MOON'S SON

534
00:56:40,147 --> 00:56:41,190
Good job, everyone.

535
00:56:42,358 --> 00:56:43,776
Song. Today's dinner--

536
00:56:43,859 --> 00:56:45,778
It was a long day for everyone.

537
00:56:45,861 --> 00:56:48,155
Get a good night's sleep,
and come in late tomorrow.

538
00:57:09,093 --> 00:57:11,846
SOME SUGGEST THAT THE LONG-LOST SON
MAY HAVE BEEN LIVING UNDER AN ASSUMED NAME

539
00:57:11,929 --> 00:57:14,306
QUESTIONS ARE MOUNTING
ABOUT CHRIS K.'S PARENTAGE

540
00:57:14,390 --> 00:57:15,558
PYEONGYEON GROUP REMAINS SILENT

541
00:57:23,607 --> 00:57:24,567
Who is that man?

542
00:57:25,901 --> 00:57:26,735
Cheonghyang.

543
00:57:27,736 --> 00:57:30,197
You said your father
told you about cheonghyang.

544
00:57:31,115 --> 00:57:32,116
Who is he?

545
00:57:35,995 --> 00:57:38,038
It didn't seem like simple anemia.

546
00:57:38,622 --> 00:57:41,041
Let's get you to a hospital for a checkup.

547
00:57:44,753 --> 00:57:46,130
I'm really okay.

548
00:57:49,466 --> 00:57:50,843
That man…

549
00:57:54,430 --> 00:57:55,431
is indeed…

550
00:57:58,184 --> 00:57:59,560
my father, Kang San.

551
00:58:00,311 --> 00:58:02,188
Why do you want to know?

552
00:58:02,771 --> 00:58:04,565
I want to know. Tell me.

553
00:58:06,650 --> 00:58:08,235
Talk to me, Chris.

554
00:58:11,530 --> 00:58:12,948
-Chris!
-That's enough, Song!

555
00:59:15,761 --> 00:59:16,762
Good job.

556
00:59:17,721 --> 00:59:20,724
It was suffocating,
lying low all this time, wasn't it?

557
00:59:22,559 --> 00:59:23,644
It's time…

558
00:59:25,604 --> 00:59:26,647
to get to work.

559
00:59:45,207 --> 00:59:46,292
What's your plan?

560
00:59:53,257 --> 00:59:54,133
This time…

561
00:59:56,885 --> 00:59:58,804
we can't let it go her way.

562
01:00:00,222 --> 01:00:01,724
You'll get hurt.

563
01:00:03,726 --> 01:00:04,643
Don't worry…

564
01:00:06,687 --> 01:00:07,563
Aunt.

565
01:01:04,286 --> 01:01:05,120
Chris.

566
01:01:10,250 --> 01:01:11,085
Chris.

567
01:01:19,218 --> 01:01:20,511
What is it?

568
01:02:21,405 --> 01:02:23,323
-It's Ms. Choi!
-Ms. Choi!

569
01:02:23,407 --> 01:02:24,867
-Ms. Choi!
-Ms. Choi!

570
01:02:24,950 --> 01:02:27,494
-You're at the heart of this controversy.
-Is Chef Chris K.…

571
01:02:27,578 --> 01:02:28,704
-Any comment?
-Ms. Choi!

572
01:02:28,787 --> 01:02:30,956
They say Chef Chris K.
is Chairwoman Moon Hae-seon's son.

573
01:02:31,039 --> 01:02:31,874
Is that true?

574
01:02:31,957 --> 01:02:33,667
He moved to the US as a pre-teen.

575
01:02:33,750 --> 01:02:36,211
Did he go with his dad after the divorce?

576
01:02:36,295 --> 01:02:37,838
Why did he leave his mother?

577
01:02:37,921 --> 01:02:39,882
Do you know why
the chairwoman abandoned him?

578
01:02:39,965 --> 01:02:42,092
-He's in there, right?
-Can we get a comment?

579
01:02:42,176 --> 01:02:43,385
-A comment, please!
-Ms. Choi!

580
01:02:43,469 --> 01:02:46,555
-Any comment?
-Please, Ms. Choi!

581
01:02:47,931 --> 01:02:48,765
Well…

582
01:03:11,455 --> 01:03:13,582
What's going on? What's all that noise?

583
01:03:15,334 --> 01:03:16,502
It's nothing.

584
01:03:17,002 --> 01:03:17,836
Nothing at all.

585
01:03:27,804 --> 01:03:28,972
It's really okay.

586
01:03:30,140 --> 01:03:31,850
Like I said, it's nothing.

587
01:03:39,149 --> 01:03:42,236
-It's Chris.
-It's Chris K.

588
01:03:42,319 --> 01:03:44,655
-Give us an interview.
-Is Kang Han your real name?

589
01:03:44,738 --> 01:03:46,657
Who named you Chris K.?

590
01:03:46,740 --> 01:03:48,242
Did you meet Chairwoman Moon in private?

591
01:03:48,325 --> 01:03:49,618
Is she your mother?

592
01:03:49,701 --> 01:03:51,828
Why did you enter the competition?
Did you have a reason?

593
01:03:51,912 --> 01:03:54,540
Did you enter knowing
Pyeongyeon's chairwoman was your mother?

594
01:03:54,623 --> 01:03:57,668
-What was the plan?
-Do you have anything to say?

595
01:03:57,751 --> 01:03:59,169
-Let's talk!
-Any comment?

596
01:04:14,059 --> 01:04:15,060
Chris!

597
01:05:18,206 --> 01:05:19,374
-Do you really think…
-Yes, Chef!

598
01:05:19,458 --> 01:05:20,542
Quick, get the olive oil.

599
01:05:20,626 --> 01:05:22,294
…his goal is to win the competition?

600
01:05:22,377 --> 01:05:23,420
About her.

601
01:05:23,503 --> 01:05:24,880
-Dad!
-Han!

602
01:05:24,963 --> 01:05:26,006
You know nothing.

603
01:05:26,089 --> 01:05:28,133
You need to hear her side of it.

604
01:05:28,216 --> 01:05:29,635
How my father…

605
01:05:29,718 --> 01:05:31,386
met his end!

606
01:05:31,470 --> 01:05:33,388
My husband. Did you kill him?

607
01:05:34,389 --> 01:05:36,683
One or the other. Which do you choose?

608
01:05:37,184 --> 01:05:39,895
I don't know
what to make of this situation.

609
01:05:40,646 --> 01:05:42,147
You, Chris…

610
01:05:43,982 --> 01:05:46,443
You're part of the Pyeongyeon Group
that killed my father.

611
01:05:50,238 --> 01:05:53,241
Subtitle: Jennifer Jean Lim
